1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,300
Section 2

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:07,200
So if you're one of those people who hasn't found the perfect physical activity

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,093
yet - here are some things to think about which might help you make

4
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:13,060
the right decision for you.

5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:18,146
The first question to ask yourself is whether you would enjoy training in a

6
00:00:18,146 --> 00:00:19,010
gym.

7
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:23,063
Many people are put off by the idea of having to fit a visit

8
00:00:23,063 --> 00:00:27,557
to the gym into their busy day - you often have to go very early

9
00:00:27,557 --> 00:00:31,670
or late as some gyms can get very crowded.

10
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:37,004
But with regular training you'll see a big difference in a relatively short space

11
00:00:37,004 --> 00:00:37,870
of time.

12
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:42,370
Running has become incredibly popular in recent years.

13
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:46,336
That's probably got a lot to do with the fact that it's a very

14
00:00:46,336 --> 00:00:51,224
accessible form of exercise - anyone can run - even if you can only

15
00:00:51,224 --> 00:00:52,946
run a few metres to begin with.

16
00:00:52,946 --> 00:00:59,983
But make sure you get the right shoes - it's worth investing in a high quality pair

17
00:00:59,983 --> 00:01:01,780
and they don't come cheap.

18
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:07,088
Another great thing about running is that you can do it at any time of day

19
00:01:07,088 --> 00:01:11,400
or night - the only thing that may stop you is snow and ice.

20
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:15,710
Swimming is another really good way to build fitness.

21
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:20,983
What attracts many people is that you can swim in an indoor pool at

22
00:01:20,983 --> 00:01:22,490
any time of year.

23
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:27,275
On the other hand, it can be quite boring or solitary - it's hard

24
00:01:27,275 --> 00:01:30,220
to chat to people while you're swimming lengths.

25
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:35,090
Cycling has become almost as popular as running in recent years.

26
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:40,216
That's probably because as well as improving their fitness, many people say being out

27
00:01:40,216 --> 00:01:45,342
in the fresh air in a park or in the countryside can be fun,

28
00:01:45,342 --> 00:01:50,468
provided the conditions are right, of course - only fanatics go out in the wind

29
00:01:50,468 --> 00:01:51,200
and rain!

30
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,870
Yoga is a good choice for those of you looking for exercise which focuses

31
00:01:56,870 --> 00:02:00,110
on developing both a healthy mind and body.

32
00:02:00,110 --> 00:02:05,605
It's a good way of building strength and with the right instructor, there's less

33
00:02:05,605 --> 00:02:09,530
chance of hurting yourself than with other more active sports.

34
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:15,332
But don't expect to find it easy - it can be surprisingly challenging, especially

35
00:02:15,332 --> 00:02:18,010
for people who aren't very flexible.

36
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:23,220
Getting a personal trainer is a good way to start your fitness programme.

37
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:27,180
Obviously there can be significant costs involved.

38
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:32,320
But if you've got someone there to encourage you and help you achieve your

39
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,890
goals, you're less likely to give up.

40
00:02:34,890 --> 00:02:39,255
Make sure you get someone with a recognised qualification, though,

41
00:02:39,255 --> 00:02:42,310
or you could do yourself permanent damage.

42
00:02:42,310 --> 00:02:47,770
Whatever you do, don't join a gym unless you're sure you'll make good use

43
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:48,550
of it.

44
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:53,406
So many people waste lots of money by signing up for membership

45
00:02:53,406 --> 00:02:55,430
and then hardly ever go.

46
00:02:55,430 --> 00:02:58,670
What happens to their good intentions?

47
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:03,252
I don't think people suddenly stop caring about improving their fitness,

48
00:03:03,252 --> 00:03:07,000
or decide they have more important things to do.

49
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,380
I think people lose interest when they don't think they're making enough progress.

50
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:19,610
That's when they give up hope and stop believing they'll ever achieve their goals.

51
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:26,981
Also, what people sometimes don't realise when they start is that it takes a lot of determination

52
00:03:26,981 --> 00:03:33,052
and hard work to keep training week after week and lots of people don't

53
00:03:33,052 --> 00:03:35,220
have that kind of commitment.

54
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:41,863
One thing you can do to help yourself is to set manageable goals - be realistic

55
00:03:41,863 --> 00:03:44,520
and don't push yourself too far.

56
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:47,014
Some people advise writing goals down,

57
00:03:47,014 --> 00:03:51,170
but I think it's better to have a flexible approach.

58
00:03:51,170 --> 00:03:56,770
Give yourself a really nice treat every time you reach one of your goals.

59
00:03:56,770 --> 00:04:01,570
And don't get too upset if you experience setbacks - it's a journey -

60
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:05,170
there are bound to be difficulties along the way.
